 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Light, flat things travel well. Dried fruit and a few biscuits would last a few days. Dried fruit would keep you. A sandwich and some dips would supplement. If you' stopping for more than two or three hours, there usually are picnic tables with water and bread. A bar, chocolate or little biscuit that fits in a pocket. Sweets go soft fast. Only if you' camping over night. For a day hike, the food in the backpack is enough.",
